 * penumbra_tests/andrill/run.php - the drill-down between Platform Metrics and
 * one report's metrics (2026-10-01, step 1 of folding report metrics into
 * Platform Metrics as a breadcrumb scope).
 *
 * Platform's report links (Most-Opened, Heaviest, Dead, the Home Visits card)
 * open analytics.php in the SAME tab carrying the window and filters; the
 * report page's sidebar crumb ("<- Platform Metrics", admins only) carries them
 * back up. (The first deploy, 2026-10-01 14:12, put it in the report strip as
 * "All reports"; the user missed the sidebar one, so it went back that day.) Both
 * directions go through ONE helper, penumbra_an_carry_params() in
 * analytics_shared.php; the crumb also read Platform's pref cookie through
 * penumbra_an_platform_prefs() for the one Platform-only checkbox - until THE
 * SWITCH (2026-10-02): analytics.php is now the engine's wrapper, a report's
 * metrics page IS analytics_all.php at report scope, which has all three
 * visibility toggles (Platform gained Hide my own views), so the drill-down and
 * the crumb carry all three both ways and the report side below emulates the
 * engine's report scope.
 *
 *   php.exe -n -d date.timezone=America/New_York run.php [--app=<dir>]
 *           [--control] [--mutant=nofs|nocmp|nodow|formonly|falsy|bareup|newtab|ungated|
 *                                 noplatform|famtheme|onecal|noexit|refreshdefault|
 *                                 noautocarry|nomeup]
 *
 * --app     defaults to the LIVE webroot; point it at a staging copy before a deploy.
 * --control adds one deliberately false assertion and MUST report FAIL 1.
 * --mutant  breaks one guarantee in the target's source and MUST turn red:
 *           nofs     the carry forgets filter_submitted (checkboxes fall back
 *                    to the receiving page's defaults / saved prefs)
 *           nocmp    the comparison is not carried
 *           nodow    the weekday scope is not carried
 *           formonly the remembered custom dates ride only while custom is on
 *           falsy    false extras are sent as an empty value (isset() reads
 *                    "excl_admins=" as ON on Platform)
 *           bareup   the crumb carries even on a bare visit (would overwrite
 *                    Platform's saved window with this page's defaults)
 *           newtab   one report link opens a new tab again
 *           ungated  the sidebar crumb shows to non-admins too
 *           noplatform the drill-down forgets platform=1 (the theme would switch)
 *           famtheme the report page never applies the family theme
 *           onecal   the one-report jump also fires in calendar mode
 *           noexit   the jump sends its header but renders the page anyway
 *           refreshdefault auto-refresh is on unless switched off
 *           noautocarry the drill-down forgets Hide automation (the way back
 *                    up would switch Platform's off)
 *           nomeup   the crumb forgets Hide my own views
 *   (since the switch bareup / ungated / famtheme / refreshdefault break the
 *   engine's report scope - analytics.php is its wrapper)
 *
 * Lifts the penumbra_an_* functions by the tokenizer (never require'd) and
 * EMULATES each page's inline filter parsing, pinning every emulated line to
 * the target source as a text anchor - if a page's parsing changes, the
 * anchor goes red and the emulation must be re-checked.
 *
 *   1. carry_params itself
 *   2. DOWN: every Platform state (address x saved prefs) -> the report page
 *      resolves the same window and filters
 *   3. UP: every chosen report-page state x ANY Platform cookie -> Platform
 *      resolves the same window, filters and toggles, and keeps its own
 *      Activity from the cookie
 *   4. DOWN then UP lands exactly where Platform was
 *   5. the cookie reader
 *   6. escaping
 *   7. page wiring (text anchors)
 *   8. a Report filter that selects ONE report opens that report's page
 *   9. the report page's theme: the family's when reached from Platform
 *      (platform=1), the report's own otherwise
 *  10. the report page's auto-refresh: off unless chosen, per browser
 *
 * EXPECTED TAIL: "PASS <n>   FAIL 0" (see the README entry for n). A smaller
 * pass count is a failure too.
 */
